skill: "community-sentiment-trends"
sections[3]:
  - "# community-sentiment-trends\n\nTrack community sentiment per channel and topic, alert on abnormal drops, and correlate them with releases and incidents. Use weekly for the standing digest, when support volume spikes, and before release so known friction is distinguished from new friction.\n\nOwner: role-community-manager (pod-customer, marketing). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[6]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - search_web\n  - web_fetch\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"channel digests (discord-automation, slack-automation exports); support ticket volume; release and incident timeline; baseline sentiment history\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/community/sentiment-trends.toon with per-channel and per-topic weekly trend, alert_flags[], correlation notes; baseline archive\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Collect channel digests through the automation exports; all page and channel fetches run through the Obscura headless engine per the browser invariant.\n2. Normalize sentiment to one scale across channels; the mapping per source is recorded so a channel's 3.0 and another's 3.0 mean the same thing.\n3. Compute the weekly trend per topic with run_command against the rolling baseline; topics are from the standing taxonomy, and new topics enter the taxonomy before they enter the report.\n4. Alert on drops beyond two baseline standard deviations; each alert names the topic, the magnitude and the window - alerts without magnitude are noise.\n5. Correlate flagged drops with the release and incident timeline; an aligned incident is labeled as incident-driven, which changes who gets the brief and what action is expected.\n6. Distinguish volume effects: a sentiment drop on tripled message volume is read differently than on flat volume; both numbers travel with the flag.\n7. Write sentiment-trends.toon and archive the baseline; brief product, support and community leads with the one-page digest, not the raw grid.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\ndigest to product, support and community leads; incident-driven flags to incident owner.\n"
